From 5eb764a10ea90d536408733a2ba240128932d41c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:07:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(contour): user-set exit point on closed 2D contours

The ring nearest links.approach.exit_point is cut all the way round,
then on along its own cutter-centre polyline to the pick's projection,
and the lead-out leaves there. A lead-out that does not fit there, a
lead-in the longer walk loses, a lead-out crossing the lead-in, tabs,
control compensation, the keep-down level link, an overlap beside it,
open chains, tilted contours and other kinds are refused by name.
Also pins the picked start's "no lead-in fits" refusal (PR 1478 review).

Refs #1473

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
